From b6351790a15d0bba0981d0d9255bd5998e6626f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:37:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 104/106] dynarmic: a persistent code cache for the A32 JIT

Jit::SaveCodeCache writes the translated code (the blocks, their cold code, the constants they
placed) and what dynarmic keeps about it: each block's guest ranges (its code and its flags
look-ahead) with a hash of that code, every link site, the fastmem fault records, and every
pointer the code holds into objects that move between runs (the JIT, the callbacks, the monitor,
the coprocessors, and UserConfig::code_cache_objects), found by scanning the code. LoadCodeCache,
before anything is translated, takes it only from the same build and configuration with the code
cache at the same address: the code is put back at the same addresses, its pointers moved to where
the objects are now, every link undone. A saved block is registered when first looked up if its
guest code still hashes the same (translated again otherwise), and linked as blocks register.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01REmpC53sSK3VTcKMxWFSSb
